  "definition": "e_L = E_cell/n: Ewald energy per particle of the periodic configuration L of unit point charges with a uniform neutralizing background, G=0 Fourier mode removed (tinfoil/periodic convention), including the background term -pi Q^2/(2 V alpha^2); units e^2/a, a = Wigner-Seitz radius. Equals W/N for the periodic jellium energy W at the perfect lattice on any commensurate torus (identity of Ewald representations). Agreement with the thermodynamic-limit jellium energy of large neutral samples built from Wigner-Seitz cells is standard (argument: the cells are neutral with vanishing dipole moment, so cell-cell interactions decay like R^-5 and the limit is shape independent; total energy of a neutral system is independent of the potential offset, so the dropped G=0 mode does not matter).",
